    {
      "name": "art-fix7 Fossil Nest doorway",
      "description": "Gibson's note 4: see-through holes in the Fossil Nest doorway. The dark opening was a 34-high panel plus a narrower 6-high arch panel, leaving two 4 x 6 notches at the top corners that looked into the house (the moss roof underside and the back wall showed through from an angle). Now one dark panel fills the opening up under the lintel and stepped stone corner blocks, sunk into the jambs and lintel, make the round top. Also two near-coplanar pairs fixed (rib knob 2 vs its rib, femur end vs nest/femur). Display point unchanged. Before close-ups: tests/hytale/golden/art-fix7/before/FossilNest_*.png; after close-ups: tests/hytale/golden/art-fix7/closeups/FossilNest_*.png.",
      "steps": [
